:0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.8.dev (7818fe4bf)\n\nBisected to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122510 CC @YeldhamDev \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (7818fe4bf) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (3840x2160 @ 120.00 Hz, 3840x2160 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running Godot inside Godot `TOOL_LIST_SELECT` option no longer shows a list. This was very useful for debugging the editor. The other options also don't work directly as the controls don't seem selectable by mouse anymore. When selecting nodes through the `Remote` scene tree the other tools work for the selected node, though changing the pivot doesn't move it to the select point but a point far away offscreen.\n\n<img width=\"857\" height=\"101\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad88e4d5-cb69-41ce-98de-070b92ec214e\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Under `Debug` -> `Customize Run Instances...` add `-e` to `Main Run Args:`\n- Run any scene (it will run the editor instead)\n- Select `2D` and test the different tool options\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_u